<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/companies-locations">Companies &amp; Locations</a> is for Admins only.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Company settings">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Company name</strong>, <strong>Theme color</strong> and a logo, shown in the menu when people
                are signed in.</li>
            <li>An optional login background image.</li>
            <li><strong>Seasonal themes</strong>: decorations in the staff app. <strong>Automatic (follow the
                calendar)</strong> shows falling snow, snow-topped cards and a string of twinkling Christmas lights on the
                card at the top of the page from 1 to 26 December, and jack-o'-lanterns in the bottom corner, the odd
                bat flying past and cobwebs on cards from 24 to 31 October (UK time). <strong>Off</strong> turns them
                off for everyone.
                <strong>Christmas (always on)</strong> and <strong>Halloween (always on)</strong> show that season
                straight away, whatever the date, so you can preview it. Set it back to Automatic afterwards.
                Press <strong>Save Changes</strong> to apply it.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            Seasonal themes never appear on kiosk screens, the clock-in terminal or the login page, and anyone can
            turn them off for themselves under <strong>Seasonal Themes</strong> on their account page. With
            reduced motion switched on in the device's settings, nothing moves: the snow stays on the cards but
            doesn't fall, the Christmas lights stay lit without twinkling, and there are no bats.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Locations">
        <FluentText>
            Each venue is a location. People sign in to one location at a time, and most management pages work
            on the location you signed in to. Add a location with <strong>New location name</strong>, set its
            <strong>Opening hours</strong>, or deactivate one you no longer use.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Features">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Features for</strong> your company switches whole modules on or off for each location, such as
            Training, Shift management, Chat, Onboarding, Announcements and Audio clips. There's a row for each
            feature and a column for each location, and a switch saves as soon as you flip it. Staff only get the
            features switched on for the location they signed in to. Turning a feature off there hides it from
            the menu, home screen and dashboards, and blocks its pages, but deletes nothing, so turning it back on
            brings everything back. Admins always see every feature.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            <strong>A new location starts with every feature off.</strong> Press <strong>All on</strong> under the
            location's name to switch everything on at once, or flip the switches you want one by one.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            Some things belong to the whole company rather than one location, such as calendar feeds,
            onboarding emails, the Audio Clips page and audio clips in automation rules. These work when at least one location has
            the feature switched on.
        </HelpNote>
        <FluentText>
            Only Lanyard's platform admins can change these switches.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Who works where">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Staff Locations</strong>: choose a person with <strong>Select User</strong> to see their
            <strong>Assigned Locations</strong>, then use <strong>Add Location</strong> or remove one. People can
            only sign in to locations they belong to, and location chat channels follow these memberships.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
